 "human_notes": {
  "_source": "guide (a transcribed 100-days run + a transcribed 'ultimate guide') + jar loot tables",
  "measured_emphasis": [
   "Across 2 transcribed guides the most-discussed mob is NOT a dragon: entity:iceandfire:hydra leads with 16 mentions, then entity:iceandfire:pixie (14), entity:iceandfire:fire_dragon (10) and entity:iceandfire:gorgon (10)",
   "That matches the advice itself — the Hydra is the fight guides feel obliged to warn about, so it deserves a prep-heavy quest rather than a footnote",
   "entity:iceandfire:pixie ranking second is a reminder that a chunk of this mod is collection and utility (iceandfire:pixie_dust), not combat",
   "iceandfire:dragonbone is the single most-named item (7) — the entry material players actually interact with, well before dragonsteel"
  ],
  "how_to_fight": [
   "entity:iceandfire:fire_dragon is the easiest of the three ONLY because a fire resistance potion negates its breath outright — the guide says so explicitly. Ice and lightning dragons have no such cheap counter and need real gear",
   "entity:iceandfire:hydra MUST be kept on fire: if it is not burning it regrows heads faster than you can cut them and the fight becomes unwinnable. Bring a Flame bow or a Fire Aspect sword. This is the single most important prep fact in the mod",
   "entity:iceandfire:gorgon kills anything that meets its gaze — wear iceandfire:blindfold. Also bring milk for its poison",
   "entity:iceandfire:siren lures you in with its song; iceandfire:earplugs are the counter",
   "entity:iceandfire:cyclops — shoot it in the eye with a bow to blind it, then close in",
   "Dragon tiers matter: stage 1-3 dragons are the surface ones, stage 4-5 live only in dragon caves and are far deadlier. Do not write one 'kill a dragon' task as if they were equivalent",
   "Only FEMALE dragons drop eggs, which is why eggs are the mod's rarest gate — a kill-a-dragon quest does not reliably yield one",
   "Dragon bones come from right-clicking a dragon skeleton found in the world, not only from a kill"
  ],
  "boss_order": [
   "entity:iceandfire:hippogryph — tameable, the guide uses it as the early mount rather than a kill",
   "entity:iceandfire:troll — the guide's first real underground scare while mining",
   "entity:iceandfire:fire_dragon — easiest and most common of the three dragons, per the guide",
   "entity:iceandfire:ice_dragon — snowy biomes, met second",
   "entity:iceandfire:lightning_dragon — the guide calls these 'the most difficult' and does them last",
   "entity:iceandfire:cyclops, entity:iceandfire:hydra, entity:iceandfire:gorgon — side bosses, not on the dragon ladder"
  ],
  "prep": [
   "The guide is blunt that iron armour 'is nothing for a dragon' — dragon-scale armour first, then dragonsteel",
   "iceandfire:bestiary is the in-game manual and the guide has to go and read it to progress (hatching, taming, the command staff) — treat it as a genuine early prerequisite",
   "Bottles before the kill: dragon blood is collected from the CORPSE with a glass bottle, ~4 per small dragon, and the guide loses hours to not having gathered it",
   "iceandfire:dragon_stick (Dragon Command Staff) / iceandfire:dragon_horn before raising a dragon — a grown untamed dragon wrecks your base"
  ],
  "order": [
   "Dragon scales -> dragon-scale armour (better than diamond)",
   "Dragon blood + a dragonforge -> dragonsteel (iceandfire:dragonsteel_fire_ingot etc.), which the guide calls stronger than netherite",
   "A dragonforge needs a LIVE chained dragon of the right element to fire it — one forge per element",
   "Eggs are RNG drops from dragons; hatching medium differs by element — fire needs flame, ice needs water, lightning needs RAIN, which the guide gets stuck waiting on"
  ],
  "key_drops": [
   "iceandfire:fire_dragon_blood / :ice_dragon_blood / :lightning_dragon_blood — the dragonsteel gate",
   "iceandfire:dragonscales_red / :dragonscales_blue / :dragonscales_electric — armour tier",
   "iceandfire:dread_key — from entity:iceandfire:dread_lich, opens the dread structures",
   "iceandfire:hydra_heart — held in the hotbar it regenerates you faster the lower your health; the guide singles it out as the best drop of the three mini-bosses",
   "iceandfire:hydra_fang -> iceandfire:hydra_arrow, which poisons and leeches life",
   "iceandfire:cyclops_eye — held in hand it weakens nearby enemies; iceandfire:gorgon_head petrifies non-undead",
   "iceandfire:blindfold and iceandfire:earplugs — cheap prep items that hard-counter the Gorgon and the Siren; good early quest rewards",
   "Sea serpent scales -> the sea-serpent armour set, which the guide values for strength plus water breathing",
   "iceandfire:deathworm_chitin_red and iceandfire:deathworm_gauntlet_red — Death Worm tier"
  ],
  "traps": [
   "iceandfire:dread_queen is NOT a spawnable entity in this build: lang key only, no loot table, no spawn egg, no kill advancement — yet iceandfire:dread_queen_sword and :dread_queen_staff exist as real items. A kill task on the Dread Queen is permanently uncompletable",
   "iceandfire:black_frost_dragon is a lang-only leftover with zero other files in the jar",
   "iceandfire:dragon_multipart, :hydra_multipart, :cylcops_multipart are hitbox segments, not mobs",
   "entity:iceandfire:cockatrice petrifies you if you meet its gaze; entity:iceandfire:gorgon turns you to stone — the guide treats both as run-away mobs",
   "Sea serpents ambush anything in open water; one guide loses a dragon to one and the other says outright not to travel by sea early",
   "Do not open the chests inside the mod's graveyards — the guide warns they are guarded by hostile ghosts, and the area is dangerous at night"
  ],
  "signature": [
   "entity:iceandfire:fire_dragon",
   "entity:iceandfire:ice_dragon",
   "entity:iceandfire:lightning_dragon",
   "iceandfire:bestiary",
   "iceandfire:dragonsteel_fire_ingot",
   "iceandfire:dragonforge_fire_core",
   "iceandfire:dragon_stick",
   "iceandfire:fire_dragon_blood"
  ]
 },
